# Project Proposal layout (SETUP Form 001)

## Scope

- **Print** is the official Form 001 via `ProjectProposalDocument` at print time (`printProjectProposalPdf`).
- **On-screen preview** in `ProjectProposalPreview.tsx` approximates Form 001 (same section order, heading indent, table columns) with portal chrome allowed (Application ID, AI/draft, signature block). Do **not** mount `ProjectProposalDocument` in the preview.
- Official PDF is still in-page print of the document, not a browser print of the preview.

## Document title

`SETUP Form 001 - Project Proposal Format`

## Indent scale

Heading and body that belong together share one wrapper. Do **not** nest `pp-form-indent-*` (paddings would add).

- **0** — cover title, section heads (`PROJECT BACKGROUND`), company-profile table, risk table
- **0.5in** (`.pp-form-indent-1`) — `A.` `B.` `C.` / `OBJECTIVES:` and narrative under those subheads
- **0.75in** (`.pp-form-indent-2`) — numbered items (`1. Organizational chart`), nested labels (`Market Situation`, Raw Material Cost)
- **1.0in** (`.pp-form-indent-3`) — dash items (`- Process Flow…`) and expected-output numbered blocks

Constants: `PP_FORM_INDENT_CLASS` / `PP_FORM_INDENT_IN`. Employee Production / Non-Production stay `.pp-form-subrow` (0.35in inside the table).

## Pagination

- Physical page footers via named `@page project-proposal-sheet`:
  - `@top-center`: `Effectivity: 2025`
  - `@bottom-center`: `SETUP Guidelines (Revision 3.0) Annex A-1: SETUP Form 001 - SETUP Project Proposal Page ` + `counter(page)` / `counter(pages)` (Arial Narrow 12pt)
- Page: A4 portrait, **1in margins** on all sides (Word `pgMar` 1440 twips).
- No per-section inline footers (avoid cross-bleed with TNA forms or fixed "Page X of 20").
- `FormBlock` + `break-inside: avoid` — section titles stay with content; long tables may break across pages.

## Print typography

Match SETUP Form 001 Word (direct formatting, not Aptos theme):

- Body / titles / section heads / cover labels: **Arial 12pt**. Title centered; section names justified.
- Subsection list items: Arial 12pt; first subsection indent **0.5in** (see Indent scale). Body text aligns with its heading — do not indent headings only.
- Tables, checkbox labels, refund months: **"Arial Narrow", Arial, sans-serif** at 11–12pt.
- Instructions (“please check appropriate box…”): Arial Narrow 12pt italic.
- Paragraph spacing after ≈ **8pt**; body line-height ≈ **1.08**. Cover fields line-height ≈ **1.15**.
- Use `pt` in print CSS (not 11px/Segoe). Table cells: ~2–4pt padding, 0.5pt black borders.

## Print path

- In-page `window.print()` via `#project-proposal-print-root` + `body.project-proposal-printing`.
- `createRoot` render (do not clone preview; do not use popup `document.write`).
- Hide portal metadata in print: no Application ID, AI/draft badges, preview signature block.

## Official sections (order)

Cover → PROJECT BACKGROUND (A. Company Profile with checkbox grids, B. Management, C. Plant site, D. Capacity, E. Raw materials) → MARKETING ASPECTS → TECHNOLOGICAL ASPECTS → WASTE MANAGEMENT → FINANCIAL ASPECT → RISK MANAGEMENT.

## Marketing (official A–F)

`PP_MARKETING_SUBHEADINGS`:

- A. Market Situation, product demand and supply
  - **Market Situation** — `marketSituation` narrative
  - **Product demand** — `productDemandSupply` narrative plus **Volume of orders** table (`volumeOfOrdersTable`): Name of company, Address, Volume of orders
  - Production / Non-Production style nesting: Product demand and the table sit under heading A; do not add a separate supply field
- B. Product specifications and product price (`productPriceTable`)
- C. Distribution channel (local/export)
- D. Competitors
- E. Existing problems (if any) — `existingMarketingProblems` (do **not** reuse S&T `interventionProblem`)
- F. Market plans/strategies

## Waste (official A–C)

A. Volume monthly / B. Kinds / C. Methods. If those three are empty, print legacy `wasteManagement` under A.

## Financial (official A–E)

`PP_FINANCIAL_SUBHEADINGS` A–E. Under **A. Financial capacity** dash item **ROI**, print the computed **Return on Investment** table (`PP_IDA_ROI_CAPTION` / `buildInvestmentDecisionAnalysis`) — Year | Annual Income (`PP_IDA_COLUMNS`). Do **not** print a separate **F. Investment Decision Analysis** section after the refund schedule.

Computed by `buildInvestmentDecisionAnalysis` (not a stored table):

- Year 1–5 annual income = frozen projection `ratios[].netIncome` (Net Income after Tax). If there is no snapshot, fall back to `form.roiTable` net-income column.
- Total = sum of those five years. Average Asset's Life = 5 (`YEAR_COUNT`). Average Income = Total ÷ 5.
- Divided by total project cost = budgetary requirement total (`sumBudgetItems`) when it is greater than 0, otherwise cover `projectCost`.
- Return on Investment = Average Income ÷ project cost, rounded to a whole percent.
- `form.roiTable` remains an editor fallback input when no projection snapshot exists; it is not printed under `- ROI`.

## Compensation table

Under **B.3 Compensation** (`3. Compensation`):

1. Seven-column table: Particulars, # of workers, Daily Rate, Days, Weekly, Monthly Salary, Annually (`PP_COMPENSATION_COLUMNS` / `form.compensationTable`)
2. Staff enter Particulars, # of workers, Daily Rate, and Days (days per week). Weekly / Monthly / Annually are computed:
   - Weekly = Daily Rate × Days × # of workers
   - Monthly = Weekly × 4
   - Annually = Monthly × 12
3. Particulars column is wide enough to show full job titles (wrap; do not clip).
4. Bold **Total** footer: Daily Rate cell is Σ(Daily Rate × workers); Days blank; Weekly / Monthly / Annually summed. Do not total Particulars or # of workers.
5. Optional narrative notes (`form.compensation`) below the table when filled

## Schedule of activities (section F)

Under **F. Schedule of activities for the proposed project**:

1. Editor is Activity plus **M1–M8** checkboxes (`form.scheduleTable`). Clients check every month the activity occupies. Do **not** collect a Timeline text column, Responsible party, or week-level checkboxes.
2. Each stored row is 9 cells: `[activity, m1…m8]`. Checked months are `"1"`. Legacy 2-col `[activity, timeline]` keeps the activity and clears months.
3. Preview (`ScheduleGanttTable` `weeksPerMonth={1}`) is a Gantt with **one cell per month** (Activity | M1–M8). A checked month fills that cell black. Print still uses 4 visual week cells per month; week cells are not separately editable.

## Existing production equipment

Editor label **Existing production equipment**. Print heading **B. Existing production equipment**. Preview and RTEC use the same 9-column snapshot (do not squash to Type / Quantity / Year).

Columns (`PP_EQUIPMENT_COLUMNS` / `form.equipmentTable`): Particulars, Year acquired, Acquisition cost, Qty, Total cost, EUL, Annual depreciation, RUL, Book Value.

Staff enter Particulars, Year acquired, Acquisition cost, Qty, EUL, RUL. Computed (read-only), straight-line with salvage 0:

- Total cost = Qty × Acquisition cost
- Annual depreciation = Total cost / EUL
- Book value = Total cost − Annual depreciation × (EUL − RUL)

If EUL is missing or ≤ 0, leave depreciation and book value blank. If RUL > EUL, treat years-used as 0 (book value = total cost).

Footer **Total** sums **Total cost** and **Book Value** only (Year, Acquisition cost, Qty, EUL, Annual depreciation, and RUL stay blank). Print as a dense 8pt fixed-layout table so 9 columns fit A4.

Legacy 3-col `[Type, Quantity, Year Acquired]` and TNA 5-col `[Type, Specs, Capacity, Units, Year]` migrate on recompute. Generated documents copy the staff/TNA grid (`equipmentTable` on the document response) and must not ask the model to invent rows.

## Capacity tables (section D)

Under **D. Capacity, volume and cost of production**:

1. Narrative (`capacityVolumeNarrative`)
2. **Raw Material Cost** (`rawMaterialCostTable` / `PP_RAW_MATERIAL_COST_COLUMNS`): Particulars, Qty, UOM, Unit Cost, Total Cost per batch, # of batches, Weekly, Monthly, Annually, Source/Supplier
   - Total Cost per batch = Qty × Unit Cost
   - Weekly = Total Cost per batch × # of batches (per week)
   - Monthly = Weekly × 4; Annually = Monthly × 12
   - Total footer sums per-batch, Weekly, Monthly, Annually
   - Print as a dense 8pt fixed-layout table so 10 columns fit A4: wrap headers (Source/Supplier), right-align money, wrap Particulars and Source — do not clip or overlap adjacent cells
3. **Raw Materials Allocation** (`rawMaterialAllocationTable`): Particulars, Ratio, Weekly — Total footer sums Ratio and Weekly

Other wide print tables (Compensation, Budget, Refund, financial ratios) use the same wrap + right-align number pattern; Budget/projections share the dense 8pt treatment.

The later **E. Raw material/s** table (`rawMaterialsTable`) is unchanged.

## Company Profile (print tables)

A. Company Profile is **one 9-column table** matching Word `tblGrid` / `vMerge` / `gridSpan` (class `pp-form-company-profile`):

- Identity: Name of Firm, Address, Contact Person, Contact No., e-mail Address, Year established, then Business Permit (number + date) as label + `colSpan={8}`
- Type of Organization: left label `rowSpan={3}` (`PP_ORGANIZATION_INSTRUCTION`). Row 1 is four checkbox+label pairs (Single Proprietorship, Partnership, Cooperative, Corporation). Row 2 is Profit + Non-Profit (`colSpan={5}`). Row 3 is Micro + Small + Medium (`colSpan={3}`). Match via `isOptionChecked()` — `Profit` must not match `Non-Profit`.
- Number of Employee: left label `rowSpan={6}` (`PP_EMPLOYEE_TABLE_CAPTION`); inner headers Type of Employment | Male | Female | Total (`colSpan={2}` each)
- Registration: left label `rowSpan={6}`; Office | Registration Number | Date of Registration. Check `isRegistrationOfficeChecked()` so DTI/SEC/CDA/LGU do not also fill Others.
- Business activities continue in the same table (empty first cell + checkbox | label `colSpan={3}` × 2) from `PP_BUSINESS_ACTIVITY_PAIRS`; RDC specify via `prioritySectorSpecify` on that cell
- Products/Services and Brief Enterprise Background as label + `colSpan={8}`

## Employee table

`Number of Employee (Please indicate number of employee)` — Type of Employment | Male | Female | Total.

- **Direct Workers** is the parent row only — print Male / Female / Total **blank** (do not copy TNA `employeesMale` / `employeesFemale` onto this row).
- **Production** shows `employeesProduction*`. If Production is empty, TNA-forwarded Direct male/female print here instead. **Non-Production** shows `employeesNonProduction*` only when those fields have values.
- The editor collects Production / Non-Production, not Direct Workers. TNA draft forwards TNA1 Direct counts into Production.
- **Indirect/Contract Workers** from `employeesIndirectMale` / `employeesIndirectFemale`. **Total** = Production + Non-Production + Indirect.

